<title>INDIA: Indian forex markets inactive due to festival.</title>
<headline>Indian forex markets inactive due to festival.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian banks are closed to observe the spring festival of Holi on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The forex market is inactive. The Indian rupee closed at 35.88/89 against the dollar on Friday, the last working day.</p>
<p>Normal market activity is expected to resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
